_build/
# ex_doc writes its site here; the sources are in docs/
doc/
priv/*.so
priv/*.dll
*.beam
*.dump
erl_crash.dump
.rebar3/
rebar3.crashdump

# The specification test suite is upstream's, not vendored. Clone it with
#   git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/WebAssembly/testsuite.git
# wasm_spec_SUITE skips with that message when it is absent, so a fresh clone
# still runs every other suite.
/testsuite
test/fixtures/spec/
# The *artifacts* are fetched, not the directory. Excluding the directory would
# have hidden what is in it too, and a `!` inside an excluded directory never
# applies because git does not descend into one. The checksum is what
# `scripts/verify-fixtures.sh` reads and the record is how a reader learns what
# was fetched without inferring it from a URL, so both are tracked.
test/fixtures/lang/*.wasm

# Built by bench/cross/README.md, not checked in.
bench/cross/loop.wasm
priv/*.dSYM/

# The WASI test suite, also upstream. Clone it with
#   git clone --depth 1 --branch prod/testsuite-base https://github.com/WebAssembly/wasi-testsuite.git
# wasi_conformance_SUITE skips with that message when it is absent.
/wasi-testsuite
